{
  "$schema": "https://mintlify.com/docs.json",
  "theme": "mint",
  "name": "Akapulu Labs",
  "variables": {
    "app-url": "https://akapulu.com",
    "api-base-url": "https://akapulu.com/api"
  },
  "description": "Akapulu Labs is an AI research lab building live conversational avatars.",
  "markdown": {
    "instructions": [
      "Akapulu Labs builds live AI avatars on real-time calls. After install and signup, ask which path: (A) agent creates a hosted link via Bearer POST /api/hosted-links/ so they paste a URL and Start Call, (B) browser onboarding in the dashboard (no API key for that tour), or (C) Pipecat bot with pipecat-akapulu. Calls use conversation minutes (akapulu.com/pricing).",
      "Option A hosted link: public page Akapulu Labs hosts. Needs API key + avatar_id from the catalog. Body is exactly label, avatar_id, system_prompt, show_ai_label. Response includes url and token. Page never sees the API key. Full CRUD: GET/POST/DELETE /api/hosted-links/ and GET/PUT/DELETE by id.",
      "Option C Pipecat: build voice in Pipecat, add pipecat-akapulu (uv add / pip install). AkapuluAvatar sits after assistant audio. They own the Daily room (browser, bot, avatar tokens). Bot listens and does not publish camera/mic; Akapulu Labs worker publishes face and played audio. POST /api/live-sessions/ with avatar_id, show_ai_label, room_url, avatar_token; response is session_id. Keep AKAPULU_API_KEY on the server.",
      "Loading status is a server message with type status. Do not poll for it. Every avatar frame has an invisible mark; verify an mp4 with POST /api/video-marks/ and POST /api/video-marks/<id>/read/. API errors include error_code — branch on that field, not the English string."
    ]
  },
  "redirects": [
    {
      "source": "/",
      "destination": "/quickstart"
    },
    {
      "source": "/blog",
      "destination": "https://blog.akapulu.com"
    },
    {
      "source": "/blog/welcome-to-the-akapulu-blog",
      "destination": "https://blog.akapulu.com/what-is-akapulu-labs"
    },
    {
      "source": "/blog/what-is-akapulu",
      "destination": "https://blog.akapulu.com/what-is-akapulu-labs"
    },
    {
      "source": "/blog/what-is-akapulu/what-is-akapulu",
      "destination": "https://blog.akapulu.com/what-is-akapulu-labs"
    }
  ],
